# enforcement-map-sites and its shard drivers (b, c, which exec the parent's run.sh --group) share ONE declaration.
# seed.sh copies core/, scripts/, .githooks/ and templates/ whole and mutates the copies; the decoy root also takes VERSION.
# The validator under test, REQUIRED: the sentinel prints where the parent run.sh passes its distribution-only guard.
!scripts/validate-enforcement-map.sh
scripts/
.githooks/
templates/
# reason: core/ is copied whole by the parent's seed this shard execs -- cp -RX "$DIST/core", core/fixtures/enforcement-map-sites/seed.sh:38.
core/
# +VERSION: VERSION is a content-key-EXCLUDED top, and the parent run.sh:3054 this shard execs copies it into the decoy root, so it is keyed per fixture (I55 arm 3).
+VERSION
core/fixtures/enforcement-map-sites/run.sh
core/fixtures/enforcement-map-sites/seed.sh
